<title>USA: U.S. factory lard use - Census.</title>
<headline>U.S. factory lard use - Census.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. factories used 29.5 million lbs of lard in edible and inedible product output in September 1996 versus a revised 33.9 million lbs in August and 35.9 million lbs in September 1995 the Census Bureau said.</p>
<p>Usage so far in the 1996 period amounted to 312.7 million lbs versus 342.9 million lbs in the 1995 period.</p>
<p>Usage includes hydrogenated vegetable and animal fats and other fats and oils in process.</p>
